== output ==
1. the end of the block closes it:
  (opened thunder_notes.txt)
  (closed thunder_notes.txt: 2 line(s) written)
  the file says: ["first", "second"]
2. so does a return, from deep inside:
  (opened thunder_trace.txt)
  (closed thunder_trace.txt: 3 line(s) written)
  first negative: -15
3. and break and continue:
  (opened thunder_round.txt)
  (closed thunder_round.txt: 1 line(s) written)
  (opened thunder_round.txt)
  (closed thunder_round.txt: 0 line(s) written)
  (opened thunder_round.txt)
  (closed thunder_round.txt: 1 line(s) written)
4. nested blocks close the innermost first:
  (opened thunder_outer.txt)
  (opened thunder_inner.txt)
  (closed thunder_inner.txt: 1 line(s) written)
  (closed thunder_outer.txt: 1 line(s) written)
5. a resource that is nothing is not closed:
  got nothing? true
6. a value made earlier can be handed to with, too:
  (opened thunder_report.txt)
